{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1793600486938652201,"compiled_state":{"alias":"average-random-piranha","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":4,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"f8a7f0ee158020b05472ddf972ce63f7177e0a13d7f6dab82c73664e1bbf3d13","event_uuid":"26578a52-79a7-44ab-82d4-82f61423b06b","position":{"commit_sha":"245a2af9779be0226759d8e767a592a3122904c6","position":"1793595372875342337-26578a52-79a7-44ab-82d4-82f61423b06b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"2f065c5166528837146f34b16ef0823e023ed573228780297b1b12bc35cbbadb","event_uuid":"354dbc16-df4d-47de-8501-a516cc30de35","position":{"commit_sha":"77775bb5adc0505fe26afcefb020f7c3c3eb558b","position":"1793595384322261374-354dbc16-df4d-47de-8501-a516cc30de35"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"4e242773e113001a994a08c9bda018759df6e3be12e50ac4129c8ea8cba64542","event_uuid":"a7f0f6f8-069b-485a-ba53-b952a9b6f656","position":{"commit_sha":"e8920b147a634b6f49ee45fc5e0db51a24318971","position":"1793595396594591204-a7f0f6f8-069b-485a-ba53-b952a9b6f656"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"35714aa82b244d5b85c6d64b0518f8a0902f1c3344bcbcdea42b4fe66d46a1b9","event_uuid":"71187d44-445b-4f7d-8417-5d246252311a","position":{"commit_sha":"c294120dceb4dde2353cc983ed223174474c54b2","position":"1793595403762442024-71187d44-445b-4f7d-8417-5d246252311a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1793595372875342337,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"354dbc16-df4d-47de-8501-a516cc30de35","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"47c8-97ac-eff3-4e88"}],"description":"## What is wrong\n\n`tests/integration/test_similar_tickets_scale.py:240`, in `test_the_cold_catch_up_cost_at_that_scale_is_emitted_as_a_number`, ends with:\n\n```python\nassert isinstance(p95, float)\nassert p95 > 0.0\n```\n\nAny wall-clock sample satisfies both unconditionally. A duration measured with a monotonic clock is a float, and it is positive. There is no behaviour of the code under test that makes this test fail — not a regression in catch-up cost, not an incorrect p95 computation, not a catch-up that silently indexes nothing. It is a measurement emitter wearing a test's name.\n\nFound by the Gerrit `LLM-Review` bot on change 3211 patchset 2 (advisory, non-blocking). No change was made under 47c8 because it was the keystone blocking three tickets and resetting its gates for a non-blocking test-naming issue was not worth the round trip.\n\n## Why it matters beyond the test file\n\nThe number this test emits is the number ADR 0122 cites as rebar's cold-catch-up p95 (ticket `weaponed-handheld-centipede`). A figure that enters the binding design record should come from something that can fail if the figure is wrong. Today nothing checks it against anything.\n\n## The two things to settle\n\n**Whether the name claims more than the body delivers.** The test is named for emitting a number, and emitting a number is what it does, so one defensible resolution is that it is correctly named and simply is not a test. The other is that a scale suite should assert something about scale.\n\n**What a non-vacuous assertion would even be.** A wall-clock ceiling is the obvious candidate and is the wrong one: 47c8 removed exactly such a budget from this file after a 500 ms criterion measured 107 ms on the development host and 545 ms on `macos-latest`. Whatever replaces the vacuous pair must be a counted invariant or a same-host ratio, consistent with how `WARM_TO_COLD_RATIO` already works at `tests/integration/test_similar_tickets_scale.py:12`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The test either asserts a property that can fail for some behaviour of the code under test, or is renamed and documented so its name does not claim to test one.\n- [ ] If an assertion is added, it is a counted invariant or a same-host ratio, not an absolute wall-clock budget. Checked by: the assertion referencing no fixed millisecond constant.\n- [ ] If an assertion is added, a test demonstrates it fails when the invariant is violated. Checked by: that test.\n- [ ] The file is swept for the same shape, so a sibling vacuous assertion is not left behind. Checked by: naming in the change what was found.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes.\n\n## Provenance\n\nCarried from the change 3211 patchset 2 review and from a comment recorded on `weaponed-handheld-centipede`, which consumes the number this test emits.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["complexity-reduction","similar-tickets"],"ticket_id":"458e-c5b2-96ef-4f8d","ticket_type":"bug","title":"The cold-catch-up scale test asserts only that a duration is a positive float, so it cannot fail","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["26578a52-79a7-44ab-82d4-82f61423b06b","354dbc16-df4d-47de-8501-a516cc30de35","a7f0f6f8-069b-485a-ba53-b952a9b6f656","71187d44-445b-4f7d-8417-5d246252311a"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793600486938652201,"uuid":"8de1e65d-902c-4f47-a804-6f1513de9a47"}